{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > README.txt <<'EOF'\nRAIDERS OF THE GOLDEN GOOSE\nFortune favours the slightly reckless.\n\nThe distributable is the named .html in the parent workspace. Open it in a\ncurrent Chromium-family browser, or serve it from localhost. The game prefers\nWebGPU and uses Three.js's WebGL2 compatibility backend when needed. Internet\naccess is required for the pinned Three.js r180 and Rapier 0.19.3 CDN modules.\nNo art, font, music, sound or voice asset downloads are used.\n\nPLAY\nLeft stick / WASD       Move\nRight stick / mouse    Aim\nSquare / left click    Whip\nR2 / right click       Shoot\nCross / Space          Jump\nCircle / Ctrl (or C)   Roll\nTriangle / E           Interact, grapple, turn a lens, exchange the idol, revive\nL2 / Shift             Sprint\nOptions / Escape       Pause\nJ                      Field journal (keyboard)\n\nCouch co-op starts with two explorers. Player two may use arrows, Enter to\njump, Shift to roll, / to whip, . to shoot, ' to interact, and 0 to sprint.\nStandard gamepads control matching seats. Additional pads join with Cross,\nup to four explorers. Xbox prompts are available in Settings.\n\nTouch: drag on the left to move; tap/drag on the right to aim and whip, hold\nto fire. Use the contextual action button for grapples, lenses and revives.\nClose combat, escape sprinting and gap jumping receive touch assistance.\n\nThe pause menu contains the field journal, settings, credits and Developer\ntoolkit. The toolkit includes live movement, jump, reach, aggression, trap,\nboulder and damage sliders; invulnerability, no clip, supplies, scene warps,\na lens solve action and defaults. Checkpoint saves stay on the device.\n\nOnline co-op is hosted by AI Hub, using its unmodified Session Protocol v1\nclient 1.4.0. All networking passes through AI Hub. The game supports 1-4\nseats, host authority, unreliable state snapshots, client input, revives,\nplayer departure, team scoring, time-up, and hosts with no local player.\nStandalone multiplayer is couch co-op; it does not require a network service.\n\nBUILD\nnode build.mjs\n\nThis joins src/*.js, src/style.css, src/shell.html, src/report.json and the\nunmodified session client into one HTML. It also writes exit-interview.json\nto the parent workspace. Runtime libraries remain external pinned CDN modules.\n\nTEST -- one command, only failures and a final count\n./tests/run.sh\n\nOptional focused suites: ./tests/run.sh --suite core|hub|visual\nThe runner starts its own 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-selected port, closes it,\nand launches one browser at a time. Browser temp files stay in this folder.\nIt uses installed Python Playwright 1.63 and exact local copies of the pinned\nruntime dependencies to avoid CDN variability during deterministic tests.\nJSON reports and visual captures are saved under artifacts/.\n\nCore tests include an ordinary-input, default-balance complete expedition\nwith all curios and a clean swap; failure/retry, saves, revives, live tuning,\ncontroller and touch emulation, the attract replay, and offline sound render.\nThe AI Hub tests use the supplied, unmodified harness in two- and four-seat\nsessions with latency, jitter and packet loss, host departure and server mode.\nVisual captures use the engine's WebGL2 diagnostic backend because headless\nWebGPU presentation can return a blank canvas even with correct game state.\n\nDeveloper instrumentation is available only with ?test=1. It exposes __GG\nfor fixed-step, ordinary-action play scripts and state snapshots, and disables\nautomatic simulation advancement so tests control time. Normal play always\nuses a 60 Hz fixed simulation. ?webgl=1 selects the compatibility backend.\n\nThe supplied source label is Raiders of the Lost Ark (1982); the particular\nedition is unknown. No internet research about the source was performed.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > README.txt <<'EOF'\nRAIDERS OF THE GOLDEN GOOSE\nFortune favours the slightly reckless.\n\nThe distributable is the named .html in the parent workspace. Open it in a\ncurrent Chromium-family browser, or serve it from localhost. The game prefers\nWebGPU and uses Three.js's WebGL2 compatibility backend when needed. Internet\naccess is required for the pinned Three.js r180 and Rapier 0.19.3 CDN modules.\nNo art, font, music, sound or voice asset downloads are used.\n\nPLAY\nLeft stick / WASD       Move\nRight stick / mouse    Aim\nSquare / left click    Whip\nR2 / right click       Shoot\nCross / Space          Jump\nCircle / Ctrl (or C)   Roll\nTriangle / E           Interact, grapple, turn a lens, exchange the idol, revive\nL2 / Shift             Sprint\nOptions / Escape       Pause\nJ                      Field journal (keyboard)\n\nCouch co-op starts with two explorers. Player two may use arrows, Enter to\njump, Shift to roll, / to whip, . to shoot, ' to interact, and 0 to sprint.\nStandard gamepads control matching seats. Additional pads join with Cross,\nup to four explorers. Xbox prompts are available in Settings.\n\nTouch: drag on the left to move; tap/drag on the right to aim and whip, hold\nto fire. Use the contextual action button for grapples, lenses and revives.\nClose combat, escape sprinting and gap jumping receive touch assistance.\n\nThe pause menu contains the field journal, settings, credits and Developer\ntoolkit. The toolkit includes live movement, jump, reach, aggression, trap,\nboulder and damage sliders; invulnerability, no clip, supplies, scene warps,\na lens solve action and defaults. Checkpoint saves stay on the device.\n\nOnline co-op is hosted by AI Hub, using its unmodified Session Protocol v1\nclient 1.4.0. All networking passes through AI Hub. The game supports 1-4\nseats, host authority, unreliable state snapshots, client input, revives,\nplayer departure, team scoring, time-up, and hosts with no local player.\nStandalone multiplayer is couch co-op; it does not require a network service.\n\nBUILD\nnode build.mjs\n\nThis joins src/*.js, src/style.css, src/shell.html, src/report.json and the\nunmodified session client into one HTML. It also writes exit-interview.json\nto the parent workspace. Runtime libraries remain external pinned CDN modules.\n\nTEST -- one command, only failures and a final count\n./tests/run.sh\n\nOptional focused suites: ./tests/run.sh --suite core|hub|visual\nThe runner starts its own 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-selected port, closes it,\nand launches one browser at a time. Browser temp files stay in this folder.\nIt uses installed Python Playwright 1.63 and exact local copies of the pinned\nruntime dependencies to avoid CDN variability during deterministic tests.\nJSON reports and visual captures are saved under artifacts/.\n\nCore tests include an ordinary-input, default-balance complete expedition\nwith all curios and a clean swap; failure/retry, saves, revives, live tuning,\ncontroller and touch emulation, the attract replay, and offline sound render.\nThe AI Hub tests use the supplied, unmodified harness in two- and four-seat\nsessions with latency, jitter and packet loss, host departure and server mode.\nVisual captures use the engine's WebGL2 diagnostic backend because headless\nWebGPU presentation can return a blank canvas even with correct game state.\n\nDeveloper instrumentation is available only with ?test=1. It exposes __GG\nfor fixed-step, ordinary-action play scripts and state snapshots, and disables\nautomatic simulation advancement so tests control time. Normal play always\nuses a 60 Hz fixed simulation. ?webgl=1 selects the compatibility backend.\n\nThe supplied source label is Raiders of the Lost Ark (1982); the particular\nedition is unknown. No internet research about the source was performed.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/audio.js';s=open(p).read();start=s.index('const melody=');end=s.index('const bins=',start);music=s[start:end];s=s[:start]+'this.scheduleMusic(phase,t);'+s[end:]\npos=s.index('  tick(phase,dt)');s=s[:pos]+'  scheduleMusic(phase,t){'+music+'}\\\\n'+s[pos:]\npos=s.index('  stop(){')\nverify=\\\"\\\"\\\"  async renderCheck(){const output={};for(const kind of ['music','effects','voices']){const ctx=new OfflineAudioContext(1,88200,44100),a=new PulpAudio();a.ctx=ctx;a.master=ctx.createGain();a.master.gain.value=.7;a.music=ctx.createGain();a.music.gain.value=.1;a.sfx=ctx.createGain();a.sfx.gain.value=.8;a.music.connect(a.master);a.sfx.connect(a.master);a.master.connect(ctx.destination);a.noise=ctx.createBuffer(1,44100,44100);const noise=a.noise.getChannelData(0),r=rngFactory(903);for(let i=0;i<noise.length;i++)noise[i]=r()*2-1;a.lastVoice=-10;a.nextNote=.05;if(kind==='music')a.scheduleMusic('escape',1.35);if(kind==='effects'){a.effect('whip');a.effect('shot')}if(kind==='voices')a.voice('Ancient warnings. Recent bullets. Promising.');const buffer=await ctx.startRendering(),samples=buffer.getChannelData(0);let energy=0,peak=0;for(const v of samples){energy+=v*v;peak=Math.max(peak,Math.abs(v))}output[kind]={rms:Math.sqrt(energy/samples.length),peak,events:a.played[kind],gain:kind==='music'?.1:.8}}return output}\\\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\ns=s[:pos]+verify+s[pos:];open(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/game.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"renderer:renderer?.backend?.isWebGPUBackend?'WebGPU':'WebGL2'\\\", \\\"renderer:renderer?(renderer.backend?.isWebGPUBackend?'WebGPU':'WebGL2'):'headless server'\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"state:audio.ctx?.state||'locked'\\\", \\\"state:audio.ctx?.state||'locked',contextTime:audio.ctx?.currentTime||0,nextNote:audio.nextNote,muted:audio.muted,masterGain:audio.master?.gain.value,musicGain:audio.music?.gain.value\\\")\n# A server owns simulation without a camera, input or GPU rendering.\ns=s.replace(\\\"function updateVisuals(dt){ambientTime\\\", \\\"function updateVisuals(dt){if(hubInfo?.server)return;ambientTime\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"if(typeof refreshPrompts\\\", \\\"if(typeof refreshPrompts\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/engine.js';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace(\\\"  renderer=new THREE.WebGPURenderer\\\", \\\"  if(\"'!AIHub.active||!AIHub.server){renderer=new THREE.WebGPURenderer\")\ns=s.replace(\"$('\"'loading').hidden=false};\\\\n  scene.add\\\", \\\"\"'$('\"'loading').hidden=false};}\\\\n  scene.add\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read().replace('let lastFrame=0,accumulator=0,frameCount=0,runtimeError=null;', 'let lastFrame=0,accumulator=0,frameCount=0,runtimeError=null,drawReady=false,warming=false;')\ns=s.replace(\\\"    await initEngine();\\\", \\\"    hubInfo=await connection;await initEngine();\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"    updateVisuals(1/60);await renderer.compileAsync(scene,camera);await renderer.renderAsync(scene,camera);\\\\n    \"'$('\"'loading').hidden=true;\\\\n    if(\"'!await initNetwork(connection))showTitle();\", \"    updateVisuals(1/60);if(!AIHub.active){await renderer.compileAsync(scene,camera);await renderer.renderAsync(scene,camera);drawReady=true}'\"\\\\n    \"'$('\"'loading').hidden=true;\\\\n    if(\"'!await initNetwork(connection))showTitle();if(hubInfo?.server)$('\"'hud').hidden=true;\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"snapshot,input:(slot=0)\\\", \\\"snapshot,offlineAudio:()=>audio.renderCheck(),input:(slot=0)\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"await renderer.renderAsync(scene,camera);return snapshot()\\\", \\\"if(renderer)await renderer.renderAsync(scene,camera);return snapshot()\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"frameCount++;controls.poll(dt);\\\", \\\"frameCount++;if(\"'!hubInfo?.server)controls.poll(dt);\")\ns=s.replace(\"renderer.render(scene,camera);requestAnimationFrame(frame);\", \"if(AIHub.active&&hubStarted&&renderer&&!warming&&!drawReady){warming=true;renderer.compileAsync(scene,