{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='src/report.json';r=json.load(open(p))\nr['sourceInformation']['testing']='112 passing automated checks: complete default-balance solo and online playthroughs, all curios, clean exchange, failure/retry, saves, live tuning, two/four couch seats, emulated standard gamepad and multitouch, assisted gap jump, offline music/effects/voice renders, unmodified AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 seats, 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss, host departure and dedicated server; visual checks at 1920×1080, 844×390 and 390×844. Physical controller, physical touch devices and real iPhone/iPad: unknown.'\nr['testingFeedback']=[\n 'Testing caught and fixed 6 game/UI/integration defects: accessible button names, a blocked escape doorway, touch attack input, attract-mode interaction range, four-seat readiness timing, and initial snapshot reliability. Additional test-driver setup issues were corrected. The final complete suite passed 112/112 checks.',\n '2 blocking defects: the escape route collider prevented completion, and cold shader warm-up caused four-seat sessions to miss the readiness deadline. Both were fixed.',\n 'The ordinary-action, default-balance whole-expedition script: it found the blocked escape and verified the lens chain, combat, all three curios, clean idol swap and victory; the same run also completed through a real shared-world session.',\n 'A single live byte-based audio-level read was least helpful: quiet 10% music rounded to silence. Separate offline renders of music, effects and voices provided measurable nonzero RMS and peak levels instead.'\n]\nr['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js combined cel materials, procedural geometry, instancing and AnimationMixer clips cleanly; Rapier supplied stable collision, jumping and movable debris.',\n 'Yes. Headless WebGPU presentation and Chromium socket-path limits needed test-driver corrections. I also initially awaited shader warm-up before Hub readiness, which missed the four-seat deadline; initialization now separates networking readiness from GPU warm-up.',\n 'The adventure state machine, traversal and combat actions, checkpoint saves, controller focus and adaptive prompts, touch assistance, and host-authoritative co-op replication.',\n 'Coordinating fixed-step Rapier simulation, native animation, cold WebGPU pipeline compilation and Hub session timing across multiple copies.',\n 'none',\n 'A first-class controller-focused game UI and character-controller integration would reduce the amount of custom infrastructure.'\n]\nr['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The concrete stack, controller-first goals, procedural audio and required developer tools gave the vertical slice a clear identity; the supplied multiplayer harness made integration verifiable.',\n 'The source is labelled 1982; whether the film or a particular game adaptation was intended is unknown. I retained the supplied label and used native knowledge of the pulp-adventure premise.',\n 'Polishing one continuous adventure across keyboard/mouse, standard gamepads, touch, couch co-op and network co-op while retaining a single-file export.',\n 'Clarify the source edition and the expected standalone multiplayer mode. Retain the developer-tool and integration-harness requirements.'\n]\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nledger={'gameDefectsFixed':[\n {'issue':'Decorative menu arrow changed accessible button names.','critical':False},\n {'issue':'Escape-corridor side wall blocked the connector.','critical':True},\n {'issue':'Touch right-hand contact did not trigger the intended attack.','critical':False},\n {'issue':'Attract replay stopped just outside the goose interaction radius.','critical':False},\n {'issue':'Awaiting cold shader warm-up missed the four-seat Hub readiness deadline.','critical':True},\n {'issue':'A lost initial snapshot left a guest without world data before host departure.','critical':False}\n], 'reviewRepairs':['Independent Left/Right Shift bindings for keyboard co-op.','Right-stick credits scrolling targets the inner scrolling region.','Touch gap assistance preserves jump momentum with partial stick input.','Checkpoint and scene warps clear one-shot animation poses.'], 'testEnvironmentNotes':['Used full Chromium with Vulkan for state-based WebGPU tests; headless WebGPU canvas screenshots are blank on this setup.','Used a relative TMPDIR within this folder to avoid Chromium Unix socket path limits.','Used a separate SwiftShader WebGL2 launch for world screenshots.','Verified procedural sound through OfflineAudioContext rather than relying on a byte-quantized live meter.'], 'finalChecks':112, 'unverified':['Physical DualSense','Real touch hardware','Real iPhone/iPad','Subjective sound quality on speakers']}\nopen('artifacts/issues-fixed.json','w').write(json.dumps(ledger,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nsed -n '1,65p' build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='src/report.json';r=json.load(open(p))\nr['sourceInformation']['testing']='112 passing automated checks: complete default-balance solo and online playthroughs, all curios, clean exchange, failure/retry, saves, live tuning, two/four couch seats, emulated standard gamepad and multitouch, assisted gap jump, offline music/effects/voice renders, unmodified AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 seats, 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss, host departure and dedicated server; visual checks at 1920×1080, 844×390 and 390×844. Physical controller, physical touch devices and real iPhone/iPad: unknown.'\nr['testingFeedback']=[\n 'Testing caught and fixed 6 game/UI/integration defects: accessible button names, a blocked escape doorway, touch attack input, attract-mode interaction range, four-seat readiness timing, and initial snapshot reliability. Additional test-driver setup issues were corrected. The final complete suite passed 112/112 checks.',\n '2 blocking defects: the escape route collider prevented completion, and cold shader warm-up caused four-seat sessions to miss the readiness deadline. Both were fixed.',\n 'The ordinary-action, default-balance whole-expedition script: it found the blocked escape and verified the lens chain, combat, all three curios, clean idol swap and victory; the same run also completed through a real shared-world session.',\n 'A single live byte-based audio-level read was least helpful: quiet 10% music rounded to silence. Separate offline renders of music, effects and voices provided measurable nonzero RMS and peak levels instead.'\n]\nr['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js combined cel materials, procedural geometry, instancing and AnimationMixer clips cleanly; Rapier supplied stable collision, jumping and movable debris.',\n 'Yes. Headless WebGPU presentation and Chromium socket-path limits needed test-driver corrections. I also initially awaited shader warm-up before Hub readiness, which missed the four-seat deadline; initialization now separates networking readiness from GPU warm-up.',\n 'The adventure state machine, traversal and combat actions, checkpoint saves, controller focus and adaptive prompts, touch assistance, and host-authoritative co-op replication.',\n 'Coordinating fixed-step Rapier simulation, native animation, cold WebGPU pipeline compilation and Hub session timing across multiple copies.',\n 'none',\n 'A first-class controller-focused game UI and character-controller integration would reduce the amount of custom infrastructure.'\n]\nr['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The concrete stack, controller-first goals, procedural audio and required developer tools gave the vertical slice a clear identity; the supplied multiplayer harness made integration verifiable.',\n 'The source is labelled 1982; whether the film or a particular game adaptation was intended is unknown. I retained the supplied label and used native knowledge of the pulp-adventure premise.',\n 'Polishing one continuous adventure across keyboard/mouse, standard gamepads, touch, couch co-op and network co-op while retaining a single-file export.',\n 'Clarify the source edition and the expected standalone multiplayer mode. Retain the developer-tool and integration-harness requirements.'\n]\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nledger={'gameDefectsFixed':[\n {'issue':'Decorative menu arrow changed accessible button names.','critical':False},\n {'issue':'Escape-corridor side wall blocked the connector.','critical':True},\n {'issue':'Touch right-hand contact did not trigger the intended attack.','critical':False},\n {'issue':'Attract replay stopped just outside the goose interaction radius.','critical':False},\n {'issue':'Awaiting cold shader warm-up missed the four-seat Hub readiness deadline.','critical':True},\n {'issue':'A lost initial snapshot left a guest without world data before host departure.','critical':False}\n], 'reviewRepairs':['Independent Left/Right Shift bindings for keyboard co-op.','Right-stick credits scrolling targets the inner scrolling region.','Touch gap assistance preserves jump momentum with partial stick input.','Checkpoint and scene warps clear one-shot animation poses.'], 'testEnvironmentNotes':['Used full Chromium with Vulkan for state-based WebGPU tests; headless WebGPU canvas screenshots are blank on this setup.','Used a relative TMPDIR within this folder to avoid Chromium Unix socket path limits.','Used a separate SwiftShader WebGL2 launch for world screenshots.','Verified procedural sound through OfflineAudioContext rather than relying on a byte-quantized live meter.'], 'finalChecks':112, 'unverified':['Physical DualSense','Real touch hardware','Real iPhone/iPad','Subjective sound quality on speakers']}\nopen('artifacts/issues-fixed.json','w').write(json.dumps(ledger,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nsed -n '1,65p' build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst { slug } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(path.join(here, \"selection.json\"), \"utf8\"));\nconst read = (f) => readFileSync(path.join(here, f), \"utf8\");\nconst report = JSON.parse(read(\"src/report.json\"));\nwriteFileSync(path.join(here, \"../exit-interview.json\"), JSON.stringify(report, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\nconst js =\n  \"const REPORT=\" +\n  JSON.stringify(report) +\n  \";\\n\" +\n  [\"engine\", \"audio\", \"world\", \"input\", \"game\", \"ui\", \"main\"].map((n) => read(\"src/\" + n + \".js\")).join(\"\\n\");\nconst html = read(\"src/shell.html\")\n  .replace(\"<!-- HUB_CLIENT -->\", \"<script>\" + read(\"hub-session.js\") + \"</script>\")\n  .replace(\"/* GAME_STYLE */\", read(\"src/style.css\"))\n  .replace(\"/* GAME_CODE */\", js.replaceAll(\"</script\", \"<\\\\/script\"));\nwriteFileSync(path.join(here, \"../\" + slug + \".html\"), html);\nwriteFileSync(path.join(here, \"game.html\"), html);\nwriteFileSync(path.join(here, \"artifacts/bundle-check.mjs\"), js);\nconsole.log(\"Built \" + slug + \".html\");\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
